        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eugene Dynkin, Vladimir Voevodsky, Nicolai V. Krylov, Fabien Morel\n- Places: Lomonosov University\n- Roles: mathematician, algebraic geometer\n- Concepts: A¹ homotopy theory\n\nFacts:\n- Eugene Borisovich Dynkin was born on 11 May 1924 and died on 14 November 2014.\n- Eugene Borisovich Dynkin was a Soviet and American mathematician.\n- Nicolai V. Krylov studied at Lomonosov University.\n- In 1966, Nicolai V. Krylov attained a doctoral candidate title at Lomonosov University under E. B. Dynkin.\n- In 1973, Nicolai V. Krylov attained a Russian doctoral degree.\n- Vladimir Alexandrovich Voevodsky was born on 4 June 1966 and died on 30 September 2017.\n- Vladimir Alexandrovich Voevodsky was a Russian mathematician.\n- Fabien Morel is a French algebraic geometer.\n- Fabien Morel was a key developer of A¹ homotopy theory with Vladimir Voevodsky.",
